From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] conhost: the first line typed shows where the cursor is

A line read keeps where its line starts (the edit line's home) from when
the read began. When Claude Code ends, its last line read is still
waiting (0794 hands the line to the next reader); the shell prints its
prompt meanwhile, and the first line typed was drawn where that dead read
had begun -- over earlier output, not after the prompt. While nothing has
been typed the line now starts where the cursor is, as Windows' console
echoes at the cursor.

Test: test/claudecon-gate.sh, ECHO (mutant SG_MUTANT_EDIT_HOME_STALE).
---
--- a/programs/conhost/conhost.c
+++ b/programs/conhost/conhost.c
@@ -1472,6 +1472,17 @@
         return STATUS_SUCCESS;
     }
 
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_EDIT_HOME_STALE
+    /* Stained Glass OS: nothing typed yet, so the line starts where the
+     * cursor is now -- output since the read began (another program's: the
+     * shell's prompt after Claude Code ended with a line read waiting) moved
+     * it, and the first line typed showed where that read had begun */
+    if (!ctx->len && (console->mode & ENABLE_LINE_INPUT))
+    {
+        ctx->home_x = console->active->cursor_x;
+        ctx->home_y = console->active->cursor_y;
+    }
+#endif
     ctx->update_begin = ctx->len + 1;
     ctx->update_end = 0;
 
